{
  "name": "Error starter · 2 Error handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Error starter · Error handler\nRuns when a workflow that names this one under **Workflow settings > Error workflow** fails in a production run (schedule, webhook, any trigger). It does not run for test runs started in the editor. Publish it.\n\nEvery failure becomes one row in `starter_error_log`. A notification is sent only for the first row with the same workflow, node and message in the current time window (60 minutes, see **Build log row**). The row is written first and the first row is read afterwards, so a burst of failures at the same moment still gives one notification.\n\n**Notify** posts `{ \"text\": \"...\" }` to `NOTIFY_URL`, the body a Slack incoming webhook takes. Swap it for a Slack or Gmail node and use `{{ $('Build log row').first().json.text }}` as the message.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 270,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "18559f0f-1e93-4abf-807d-44ceb55042db",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "1da9f26a-0f8a-4634-8a50-6897ea1dc6a3",
      "name": "Error Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const NOTIFY_URL = 'https://example.com/your-webhook';\nconst THROTTLE_MINUTES = 60;\n\n// A failed run arrives with `execution`; a trigger that could not start\n// arrives with `trigger` instead.\nconst event = $input.first().json;\nconst error = event.execution?.error ?? event.trigger?.error ?? {};\nconst workflow = event.workflow?.name ?? '';\nconst node = event.execution?.lastNodeExecuted ?? error.node?.name ?? '';\nconst message = error.message ?? 'Unknown error';\nconst execution_url = event.execution?.url ?? '';\n\n// Same workflow, node and message in the same window: same key.\nconst window = Math.floor(Date.now() / (THROTTLE_MINUTES * 60000));\nconst throttle_key = [event.workflow?.id ?? '', node, message, window].join('|');\n\nconst text = `n8n: \"${workflow}\" failed at \"${node}\": ${message}${execution_url ? ` ${execution_url}` : ''}`;\nreturn [{ json: { workflow, node, message, execution_url, failed_at: new Date().toISOString(), throttle_key, text, notify_url: NOTIFY_URL } }];"
      },
      "id": "526589ff-cd5b-4f81-846d-6f86df0c8e33",
      "name": "Build log row",
